    <!-- Tab introductions: plain words, no acoustics terms (NFR-2) -->
    <string name="room_intro">Describe the room: its size, the rows and columns of seats, and what the walls and floor are made of. You can also load a sample room to explore.</string>
    <string name="measure_intro">Find out how clearly people can hear at each seat. You clap at the front while the phone listens at a few seats, then it checks the background noise.</string>
    <string name="results_intro">After measuring, you\'ll see which seats can follow the speaker, and whether echo, noise or distance is the problem.</string>
    <string name="fixes_intro">Try cheap changes before spending money: curtains, switching off fans, moving the speaker or using a microphone. ClearRoom predicts how much each one helps.</string>
    <string name="log_intro">Leave the phone in the room to see how background noise changes through the day. Only sound levels are kept, never audio.</string>

